src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T23:03:14-07:00","id":979525,"title":"","content":"Boar never fell to the Wyrm, and yet his children the Grondr never came back. I don't think it's possible for the extinct to come back. If they were, it would seem like cheating and actually inappropriate for a game whose themes include that nature is precious and we should be careful. If the Camazotz could come back, why not the dodo bird or passenger pigeon? They can't because in real life they are gone - gone forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:13:25-07:00","id":979538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/979450-bats-redemption?p=979525#post979525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boar never fell to the Wyrm, and yet his children the Grondr never came back. I don't think it's possible for the extinct to come back. If they were, it would seem like cheating and actually inappropriate for a game whose themes include that nature is precious and we should be careful. If the Camazotz could come back, why not the dodo bird or passenger pigeon? They can't because in real life they are gone - gone forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on the fence with this statement. I agree that once an animal species is extinct that is it for any breed associated with them. Sorry Khara, Apis, and Grondr. That is the real reason that the Grondr aren't still around at least according to CB20 modern &quot;wild boars&quot; are actually domesticated swine that have gone feral. Personally I'd rule the Red Talons mating with dingoes was impossible, but hey I'm just a player.<br /> <br /> The Camazotz however are a special case in this discussion, The Camazotz like the Corax rely on a rite not breeding. Bats are still going strong and the Camazotz are simply lacking the spirtual power to fuel the rite. Bat while returned is split into two perhaps Bat servant of Gaia doesn't have the energy to fuel the rite meaning the Camazotz are lost forever. <br /> <br /> Barriers to the Camazotz returning:<br /> Bat lacks the spiritual energy to empower the rite.<br /> The remaining Camazotz are so deep in the Umbra they do not hear his call.<br /> The Camazotz have been in the Umbra so long they can no longer cross the Gauntlet to perform the rite.<br /> None of the surviving Camazotz spirits/survivors know the rite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:16:58-07:00","id":979602,"title":"","content":"CB20 also offers suggestions to the return of the Grondr or Apis.<br /> <br /> So &quot;Gone is Gone&quot; may be the default, but you cant slap someone down for wanting to go against it.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless reason Camazotz are a special case to me, is a random confluence of genetics wont revive them.<br /> <br /> Nor could some Scientist trying to ressurect their species.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also note, the Mokole survived the EXTINCTION of their original species, so I think that puts a pretty big hole in your theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpa